    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d222">

                <pb facs="0358" n="266" xml:id="pg266"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Porter to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-02-24"><hi rendition="#italic">February 24,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 427.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to Mr. Vignaud’s No. 420, of
                    February 13, concerning the citizenship of Mr. Gendrot, I have now to report
                    that his case came up before the second council of war on the 18th instant, and
                    that upon the application of his lawyer—a lawyer given him by the court—it was
                    postponed in order to give Gendrot time to have the question of his nationality
                    decided by a civil court. Gendrot’s lawyer informs this embassy that if no step
                    of this kind is taken his client will be brought up again before the military
                    court, where he is sure to be sentenced to imprisonment and be obliged to serve
                    some time in the French army.</p>
                <p>I inclose herewith copy of a letter received from Gendrot, in which he claims the
                    protection of this embassy as an American citizen and asks to be provided with
                    the necessary means for bringing before a French civil court the action without
                    which his rights will not be respected.</p>
                <p>I respectfully ask for authorization to comply with this request.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Horace Porter.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d222-a1.xml" xpointer="d222-a1"/>
            </div>
